// Syncthing ignore rules for the Sunny vault.
//
// Audited 2026-09-23. The vault was 10MB, of which ~144KB (1.4%) was
// actual notes. All 19 conflict files on record came from machine churn
// or Obsidian's own per-device state -- NOT ONE came from a note edited
// in two places. Conflicts by device: laptop 8, sunshine-m700 8 (Sunny
// itself), Keaton-PC 3, iPad 0.
//
// So the fix is not a different sync tool. It is not syncing the 9.8MB
// that has no business being synced.
//
// This file is NOT synced between devices -- keep the copies on
// Keaton-PC and sunshine-m700 in step by hand when editing.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Obsidian's own state. 12 of the 19 conflicts, and 4.6MB.
// workspace.json records which panes are open, so it differs per device
// by definition and is rewritten constantly. Plugin data.json is a local
// cache. Syncing any of it guarantees conflicts forever.
// Decision (2026-09-23): ignore the lot. Installing a plugin three times
// is cheaper than this class of conflict existing at all.
.obsidian

// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Sunny's append-only logs. 4.5MB, including a 3.98MB suggestions.md,
// rewritten continuously on the server and read on no other device.
// health_check.py:97 and sensors.py:28 already exclude this directory
// from what counts as "knowledge" -- the classification existed, it just
// was never wired to the sync boundary.
// Longer-term these move out of the vault entirely; until then, ignored.
log

// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Runtime cursors, rewritten every few minutes by the sensor loop.
// Pure machine state: position markers, not content.
data/state/*cursor*.json
data/state/health-check.md

// Mirror of scheduled.db. The file says so in its own header: "the real
// data lives in SQLite, not here". Regenerated on every change, and the
// source of one of the 19.
data/state/alarms-reminders.md

// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Stale top-level state/ tree, superseded by data/state/ in a path
// migration. Files last touched 2026-08-27. Left on disk deliberately
// rather than deleted -- ignoring it stops the churn, and deleting
// someone else's leftovers is their call to make.
state

// ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Syncthing's own furniture, and the wreckage of past conflicts.
// (?d) lets Syncthing delete these when it needs the directory gone,
// instead of refusing and leaving a half-removed tree behind.
.stfolder
(?d).stversions
(?d)*.sync-conflict-*

// Editor and OS noise.
(?d).DS_Store
(?d)Thumbs.db
(?d)desktop.ini
*.tmp
*~
